Subject: [PATCH] generic-pc: do not touch host disks during startup

The receiver startup path applies hdparm/hd-idle settings to its expected
embedded disks before entering CNeutrinoApp::RealRun().  On a Linux PC this
can probe unrelated host disks, fail with permissions, or delay the GUI.
Generic-PC keeps the HDD menu and recording support; only this automatic
receiver startup action is omitted.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific startup policy]

--- a/src/neutrino.cpp
+++ b/src/neutrino.cpp
@@ -2499,9 +2499,11 @@ int CNeutrinoApp::Run(int argc, char **argv)
 
 	InitZapper();
 
+#if !defined(HAVE_GENERIC_HARDWARE)
 	CHDDDestExec * hdd = new CHDDDestExec();
 	hdd->exec(NULL, "");
 	delete hdd;
+#endif
 
 	hintBox->hide(); // InitZapper also displays a hintbox
 	delete hintBox;
